    "q-270890": {
      "dom_id": "step-q270890",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "The function $f(x),$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3x+k}},\\,x\\ne -\\frac{k}{3}\n$$\n\nhas an inverse function given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8}{3{x}^{3}}-\\frac{5}{3},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3x+k}}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3y+k}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3y+k}} \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{3y+k} & =\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ {(\\sqrt[3]{3y+k})}^{3} & ={(\\frac{2}{x})}^{3} \\\\ 3y+k & =\\frac{{2}^{3}}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ 3y & =\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}-k \\\\ 3y & =\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}-k \\\\ y & =\\frac{8}{3{x}^{3}}-\\frac{k}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8}{3{x}^{3}}-\\frac{k}{3},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-\\frac{k}{3}=-\\frac{5}{3}\\,⟹\\,k=5.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
